s390/entry: Make pgm_check_handler() ready for lowcore relocation

jira KERNEL-1869
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-741.7.1.el9_9
commit-author Sven Schnelle <svens@linux.ibm.com>
commit 9e1e275fa28d5896ca7cdf8afa5eb58c0117a303
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-741.7.1.el9_9/9e1e275f.failed

In preparation of having lowcore at different address than zero,
add the base register to all lowcore accesses in pgm_check_handler().

	Reviewed-by: Heiko Carstens <hca@linux.ibm.com>
	Signed-off-by: Sven Schnelle <svens@linux.ibm.com>
	Signed-off-by: Vasily Gorbik <gor@linux.ibm.com>
(cherry picked from commit 9e1e275fa28d5896ca7cdf8afa5eb58c0117a303)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	arch/s390/include/asm/lowcore.h
#	arch/s390/kernel/entry.S
diff --cc arch/s390/include/asm/lowcore.h
index 94f954250ae0,183ac29afaf8..000000000000
--- a/arch/s390/include/asm/lowcore.h
+++ b/arch/s390/include/asm/lowcore.h
@@@ -227,4 -236,19 +227,22 @@@ static inline void set_prefix(__u32 add
  	asm volatile("spx %0" : : "Q" (address) : "memory");
  }
  
++<<<<<<< HEAD
++=======
+ #else /* __ASSEMBLY__ */
+ 
+ .macro GET_LC reg
+ 	ALTERNATIVE "llilh	\reg,0",					\
+ 		__stringify(llilh	\reg, LOWCORE_ALT_ADDRESS >> 16),	\
+ 		ALT_LOWCORE
+ .endm
+ 
+ .macro STMG_LC start, end, savearea
+ 	ALTERNATIVE "stmg	\start, \end, \savearea",				\
+ 		__stringify(stmg	\start, \end, LOWCORE_ALT_ADDRESS + \savearea),	\
+ 		ALT_LOWCORE
+ .endm
+ 
+ #endif /* __ASSEMBLY__ */
